    "body": "It looks like we are running `Context::new()` every time?\r\nPerhaps this is premature but it could be a good idea to chuck the Context struct on the heap and return a reference instead? try to only it initialize once and then reuse across re-renders since i'm pretty sure its read-only anyway? \r\n\r\nCould make it easy to do the caching you were talking of but then we have to think about invalidation which is a whole thing. \r\n\r\nAnyway just a thought, something we could look into later.",
    "created_at": "2019-04-26T18:09:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-04-26T18:23:48Z",
