    "body": "> It looks like we are running Context::new() every time?\r\n> Perhaps this is premature but it could be a good idea to chuck the Context struct on the heap and return a reference instead?\r\n\r\nI'm not sure I understand. `Context::new()` should only be running once in `print.rs` every time the whole prompt is being rendered. The only time context is used is by the reference passed here to generate the modules:\r\nhttps://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/print.rs#L30\r\n\r\nI was hoping to eventually implement some form of caching that would persist between calls to `starship`, but yeah, that will end up being complicated.",
